{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791668718,"nonce":"shyZtUkdqdMpSQSmy7NJjnYVQNQ=","title":"Comment placeholders were counted as siblings by structural selectors","message":"Host.createComment made a layout node and never described it to the cascade, and the cascade counts any node with no element as a sibling. A framework's placeholder before an element made it not :first-child, and shifted every :nth-child after it.\n\nReproduced: a row with a comment, an element, a comment, an empty text and two more elements matched :first-child on none and :nth-child(2) on the first element. Text was already described as anonymous, so it never counted.\n\nFix: a comment is registered as an anonymous element, as text is. tests/native-css.mjs checks :first-child, :nth-child and :last-child behind placeholders, and that they take no room (display: none, so no gap either). Vue's renderer and the JSX runtime's regions both depend on this.","files":null}]}